herald (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial release.
  * Two display surfaces: terminal greeting (/etc/profile.d) and login
    MOTD (/etc/update-motd.d). Both off by default; toggle with
    'herald terminal', 'herald motd', or 'herald all'.
  * Quote source: zenquotes.io with 1.5s timeout, fallback to a local
    pool of ~30 quotes shipped in /usr/share/herald/quotes.json.
  * Cache at /var/cache/herald/today.json, refreshed by a systemd timer
    (every three hours by default; configurable via 'herald set-refresh').
  * Optional /etc/herald.prefix prepended above the quote.
  * Suggests update-motd (not Recommends) so laptop users who only want
    the terminal greeting don't pull in extra packages by default.

